From: Chimera core
Subject: [PATCH] a read of the controls is told to the core

With SUPERMODEL_CHIMERA, every read of the Model 3's input registers
(0xF0040000: the switch banks, the analog channels, the light gun and
the serial ports of the control panel) tells the core, which counts a
frame in which none was read as a lag frame.
---
--- a/Src/Model3/Model3.cpp
+++ b/Src/Model3/Model3.cpp
@@ -243,11 +243,19 @@
  Game controls. The EEPROM is mapped here as well.
 ******************************************************************************/
 
+#ifdef SUPERMODEL_CHIMERA
+extern "C" void chimera_inputs_read(void);
+#endif
+
 UINT8 CModel3::ReadInputs(unsigned reg)
 {
   UINT8 adc[8];
   UINT8 data;
   reg &= 0x3F;
+#ifdef SUPERMODEL_CHIMERA
+  // the game looked at its controls: this frame is no lag frame
+  chimera_inputs_read();
+#endif
   switch (reg)
   {
   case 0x00:  // input bank
